WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:02.302
-Thank you for being
in the studio, pal.

00:00:02.302 --> 00:00:03.736
There's lots to talk about.

00:00:03.736 --> 00:00:06.772
Congrats, first of all,
on being on "Dear Evan Hansen"

00:00:06.772 --> 00:00:09.075
and getting crazy good reviews.
You're fantastic.

00:00:09.075 --> 00:00:11.044
-Thanks. Thank you so much.

00:00:11.044 --> 00:00:13.212
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:13.212 --> 00:00:15.114
-We have this big project
we have to talk about,

00:00:15.114 --> 00:00:17.417
but first off
I want to say how charming

00:00:17.417 --> 00:00:19.285
and cute were your parents.

00:00:19.285 --> 00:00:21.887
I just met backstage.
-Yeah. I love them so much.

00:00:21.887 --> 00:00:23.690
I'm so happy that they're here!

00:00:23.690 --> 00:00:25.725
-Do they come
to all your stuff?

00:00:25.725 --> 00:00:26.926
-Yes, all the time.

00:00:26.926 --> 00:00:28.161
-They do?
-They're very supportive.

00:00:28.161 --> 00:00:29.895
I love them very much.
-I love them.

00:00:29.895 --> 00:00:31.497
Now you're doing this new film.

00:00:31.497 --> 00:00:33.233
You're about to go to Italy
or no?

00:00:33.233 --> 00:00:34.800
Where are you doing this?
-I just came from Italy.

00:00:34.800 --> 00:00:36.202
-Okay, and you're
about to do this new film.

00:00:36.202 --> 00:00:37.436
-And now I'm going to go
to Australia.

00:00:37.436 --> 00:00:39.505
-Australia. Wow.
-Yes.

00:00:39.505 --> 00:00:42.241
-And who are playing
your parents in this film?

00:00:42.241 --> 00:00:45.378
-George Clooney and Julia
Roberts are playing my parents.

00:00:45.378 --> 00:00:48.647
-Yeah, not bad. That's --
That's pretty awesome.

00:00:48.647 --> 00:00:51.784
I mean,
are your parents psyched?

00:00:51.784 --> 00:00:53.619
They're like,
"This is perfect casting."

00:00:53.619 --> 00:00:56.222
-I mean, it is truly. I mean --

00:00:56.222 --> 00:00:59.792
But they're also just like,
"Meh. That's cool."

00:00:59.792 --> 00:01:01.561
-Really? Really?
They just do that?

00:01:01.561 --> 00:01:03.496
-They're just very chill
about it, yeah.

00:01:03.496 --> 00:01:04.931
-Last time we talked,
you told me

00:01:04.931 --> 00:01:06.633
that you were in a band
with your sister.

00:01:06.633 --> 00:01:07.866
-Yes.

00:01:07.866 --> 00:01:09.635
-All right? And you're
about to release music.

00:01:09.635 --> 00:01:13.506
-We are. We've been working on
an EP for a good while.

00:01:13.506 --> 00:01:15.908
We kind of got stopped
because of the pandemic.

00:01:15.908 --> 00:01:17.343
But we're releasing new music.

00:01:17.343 --> 00:01:19.212
-And the name of your band
with your sister

00:01:19.212 --> 00:01:20.713
was Beulahbelle.

00:01:20.713 --> 00:01:23.283
-Yes, Beulahbelle
is the current name.

00:01:23.283 --> 00:01:24.951
-It's the current name.
Beulahbelle.

00:01:24.951 --> 00:01:27.319
-Yes. Beulahbelle. You're having
trouble saying it already.

00:01:27.319 --> 00:01:29.288
-I am, yes.
But you want to change it --

00:01:29.288 --> 00:01:30.956
-That's why we want
to change it.

00:01:30.956 --> 00:01:33.492
No can spell it.
No one can say it.

00:01:33.492 --> 00:01:35.261
And we just want
something fresh.

00:01:35.261 --> 00:01:36.396
-Fresh.

00:01:36.396 --> 00:01:37.831
-Yeah, we just need
something fresh.

00:01:37.831 --> 00:01:39.598
And it's also, like, the last
time we can change it, too,

00:01:39.598 --> 00:01:41.568
because we've changed it,
like --

00:01:41.568 --> 00:01:43.503
This will be the fourth time
we change it.

00:01:43.503 --> 00:01:44.971
But this is --
We can't do it anymore.

00:01:44.971 --> 00:01:46.806
-We can crack this tonight.
-Oh, you're going to come up --

00:01:46.806 --> 00:01:48.474
-Yeah, I'm going to come up
with your name, yeah.

00:01:48.474 --> 00:01:51.143
Because it's Kaitlyn Dever.
What's your sister's name?

00:01:51.143 --> 00:01:52.845
-Maddie Dever.
-Maddie Dever.

00:01:52.845 --> 00:01:54.747
-We can't be, like,
the Dever Sister.

00:01:54.747 --> 00:01:56.315
That's not gonna work.

00:01:56.315 --> 00:01:58.251
-Deeves.

00:01:58.251 --> 00:02:00.353
-Deeves?!

00:02:00.353 --> 00:02:04.490
People do call me "Deeves."
That's -- That's good.

00:02:04.490 --> 00:02:07.193
[ Laughter ]

00:02:07.193 --> 00:02:09.095
-People call me "Deeves."
Call ma Deeves.

00:02:09.095 --> 00:02:11.330
How about Ma Deeves?
-Ma Deeves?

00:02:11.330 --> 00:02:14.367
-Yeah. Ma Deeves.
Madea. Madea.

00:02:14.367 --> 00:02:17.903
-No! This is terrible.
-No. She's you're sister.

00:02:17.903 --> 00:02:19.239
-Ma Deeves? Ma Deeves.

00:02:19.239 --> 00:02:21.341
-Dever. How about Seesters?

00:02:21.341 --> 00:02:22.742
-Seester?

00:02:22.742 --> 00:02:23.942
[ Laughter ]

00:02:23.942 --> 00:02:25.311
-"This is my seester."

00:02:25.311 --> 00:02:27.747
[ Laughter ]

00:02:27.747 --> 00:02:29.749
Seesters is the name
of the band.

00:02:29.749 --> 00:02:31.917
Like Friendster.
S-E-E-S-T-E-R. Seester.

00:02:31.917 --> 00:02:33.352
-No "The."
-No.

00:02:33.352 --> 00:02:34.921
-Just Seester.
-Seester. That's the name.

00:02:34.921 --> 00:02:36.422
Congratulations.
-I'll run it by Maddie.

00:02:36.422 --> 00:02:37.690
Thank you.
-Yeah, no problem.

00:02:37.690 --> 00:02:39.659
-I'll run it by her.
-If you ever need my help...

00:02:39.659 --> 00:02:43.062
[ Applause ]

00:02:43.062 --> 00:02:44.730
You sing,
but you also play the guitar.

00:02:44.730 --> 00:02:46.365
-Yeah.
-Do you remember your first song

00:02:46.365 --> 00:02:47.834
you played on the guitar?

00:02:47.834 --> 00:02:49.936
-It was "Crazy Train"
by Ozzy Osbourne.

00:02:49.936 --> 00:02:51.104
-Wow!

00:02:51.104 --> 00:02:52.972
-Difficult. Difficult stuff.

00:02:52.972 --> 00:02:56.709
[ Imitating guitar melody ]
Wow.

00:02:56.709 --> 00:02:58.310
-Yeah. That was good.
-Thank you.

00:02:58.310 --> 00:03:01.213
Were you into heavy metal?

00:03:01.213 --> 00:03:02.682
-I had a phase.

00:03:02.682 --> 00:03:04.150
I had, like,
a Criss Angel phase.

00:03:04.150 --> 00:03:06.152
I had, like, a real --
And I say it was a phase,

00:03:06.152 --> 00:03:07.587
but then I go back and realize

00:03:07.587 --> 00:03:10.756
that it was kind of a long time
that I liked these things.

00:03:10.756 --> 00:03:12.926
-I want to talk about --

00:03:12.926 --> 00:03:15.094
I wanna talk about "Dopesick."
-Yeah.

00:03:15.094 --> 00:03:18.831
-This is based on a true story.
It's an insane story.

00:03:18.831 --> 00:03:21.800
I know Michael Keaton
is a producer, as well,

00:03:21.800 --> 00:03:23.002
and co-stars with you.

00:03:23.002 --> 00:03:25.171
But it's basically
about the opioid crisis.

00:03:25.171 --> 00:03:28.241
-Yeah, opioid crisis
that began in the '90s,

00:03:28.241 --> 00:03:31.844
and we follow the Purdue Pharma,
Sackler family story line,

00:03:31.844 --> 00:03:35.181
but we also follow
the doctors and victims

00:03:35.181 --> 00:03:37.216
of the crisis, as well,
and it's --

00:03:37.216 --> 00:03:39.686
-It's just a scary thing.
-It's really crazy.

00:03:39.686 --> 00:03:41.754
-OxyContin.

00:03:41.754 --> 00:03:43.823
It's like just, "Yeah.
Just get it. Just take it.

00:03:43.823 --> 00:03:45.424
It's not addictive."

00:03:45.424 --> 00:03:47.693
-But not a lot of people knew
about what was going on,

00:03:47.693 --> 00:03:48.928
especially at that time.

00:03:48.928 --> 00:03:50.629
But even now, like,
I have so many friends

00:03:50.629 --> 00:03:53.132
that didn't know about,
like, the real truth.

00:03:53.132 --> 00:03:56.602
And this -- our show is going
to reveal a lot of things.

00:03:56.602 --> 00:03:59.238
-How was Michael Keaton
to work with?

00:03:59.238 --> 00:04:01.107
-Ohh.
-Difficult.

00:04:01.107 --> 00:04:04.811
-He's -- No, really
just the sweetest man.

00:04:04.811 --> 00:04:07.813
He's truly, like,
a bucket-list actor for me.

00:04:07.813 --> 00:04:10.616
I can't even tell you.
I mean, I've watched --

00:04:10.616 --> 00:04:11.850
Obviously the classics

00:04:11.850 --> 00:04:13.686
are, like,
"Batman," "Beetlejuice."

00:04:13.686 --> 00:04:16.088
Everybody knows those, right?
The classics.

00:04:16.088 --> 00:04:17.523
-Of course. Yeah.

00:04:17.523 --> 00:04:21.761
-But what shaped me as a person
growing up was the film --

00:04:21.761 --> 00:04:23.930
I don't know if you've seen
it -- called "Jack Frost."

00:04:23.930 --> 00:04:26.665
-Wow! That's your
Michael Keaton go-to?

00:04:26.665 --> 00:04:28.701
-That's my go-to.

00:04:28.701 --> 00:04:30.069
-"Jack Frost" was --
-"Jack Frost."

00:04:30.069 --> 00:04:31.704
-It's where he turned into
a snowman, right?

00:04:31.704 --> 00:04:33.438
-Man turned snowman.
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:04:33.438 --> 00:04:34.807
-With eyebrows.

00:04:34.807 --> 00:04:36.609
-Did he get hit by a car
or struck by lightning?

00:04:36.609 --> 00:04:37.843
-Michael Keaton eyebrows.
What?

00:04:37.843 --> 00:04:39.545
-Did he get struck by lightning
or something?

00:04:39.545 --> 00:04:41.347
-Yeah, it's --
-And he turns into a snowman?

00:04:41.347 --> 00:04:42.614
-Yeah, you remember.

00:04:42.614 --> 00:04:46.218
-Yeah, and he raises
his children as a snowman.

00:04:46.218 --> 00:04:48.387
I kind of remember this,
but that's the one?

00:04:48.387 --> 00:04:49.855
-Yes, you got to go back.

00:04:49.855 --> 00:04:51.423
Skip "Beetlejuice."
Skip "Batman."

00:04:51.423 --> 00:04:53.725
Go back to "Jack Frost."
-That's not true at all.

00:04:53.725 --> 00:04:55.761
He's done so many great things.

00:04:55.761 --> 00:04:58.364
You know what I love about him?
Is that he loves comedy.

00:04:58.364 --> 00:05:00.566
He actually, like,
is a student of comedy.

00:05:00.566 --> 00:05:02.869
He loves to do bits and --

00:05:02.869 --> 00:05:04.803
-He was great. I loved him.

00:05:04.803 --> 00:05:06.939
It's really shocking that
I'm in the same show as him.

00:05:06.939 --> 00:05:08.608
It's really mind-blowing to me.

00:05:08.608 --> 00:05:10.809
-Then George Clooney,
then Julia Roberts,

00:05:10.809 --> 00:05:12.912
and now this.
-And now this.

00:05:12.912 --> 00:05:15.748
-This is what I'm talking about.
Come on.

00:05:15.748 --> 00:05:18.517
I want to show this. Hopefully
your seester's watching.

00:05:18.517 --> 00:05:20.286
-[ Laughter ]
-Everyone, here is

00:05:20.286 --> 00:05:22.722
Kaitlyn Dever and Michael Keaton
in "Dopesick."

00:05:22.722 --> 00:05:24.957
Take a look at this.
-You're not the first person

00:05:24.957 --> 00:05:26.592
who can't sleep
through the night.

00:05:26.592 --> 00:05:28.794
That's not uncommon.

00:05:28.794 --> 00:05:31.998
So, I got two options.

00:05:31.998 --> 00:05:35.101
We can, uh, switch you
to a different medication.

00:05:35.101 --> 00:05:38.170
-No, I-I don't want to switch.

00:05:38.170 --> 00:05:41.240
This works better than anything
I've ever used before.

00:05:41.240 --> 00:05:43.309
-Okay. Well, option two is

00:05:43.309 --> 00:05:45.378
I can double your dose
to 20 milligrams.

00:05:45.378 --> 00:05:47.680
But if that doesn't work,
I'm gonna switch you

00:05:47.680 --> 00:05:49.648
to something else.

00:05:49.648 --> 00:05:51.750
And, uh, if you're still
having a hard time

00:05:51.750 --> 00:05:53.619
sleeping through the night,
you call me.

00:05:53.619 --> 00:05:56.021
And if you don't call me...

00:05:56.021 --> 00:05:58.958
-Then you'll call me.
-That's correct.

00:05:58.958 --> 00:06:01.160
-Mm! Kaitlyn Dever.

00:06:01.160 --> 00:06:04.430
"Dopesick" premieres
October 13th on Hulu.

00:06:04.430 --> 00:06:07.533
Hi, Mom and Dad.
You've got to be very proud.

